.claude/settings.json:183:        "_comment": "Canonical-edit sentinel (Sprint 5 Phase 7 ADR-010 + PLAN-065 Layer A 2026-05-04): blocks Edit/Write/MultiEdit AND any mcp__* tool with write-shaped params (path/file_path/content/patch/diff/source/text) against canonical governance paths unless a matching Owner-signed sentinel exists. Layer A closes S81-tris gap: custom MCP tools (mcp__codex__apply_patch etc.) previously bypassed the gate entirely. See feedback custom_mcp_tools_governance_gap.md.",
.claude/settings.json:231:        "_comment": "Arbitration-kernel HARD-DENY (PLAN-019 P1-SEC-A + PLAN-065 Layer A 2026-05-04): blocks Edit|Write|MultiEdit AND any mcp__* tool with write-shaped params on the hooks that enforce governance themselves + _lib policy/redact/audit-emit/contract primitives + .claude/policies. NO sentinel escape — only CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE=<reason-slug> + CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT bypasses (bypass emits veto_triggered audit event with reason_code=kernel_override_used). Layer A closes S81-tris gap on kernel-protected paths.",
.claude/settings.json:337:        "_comment": "PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection. BLOCKING (maintainer ceremony). Allows first-time CREATION of a config (ENOENT) but BLOCKS any Edit/Write/MultiEdit that MODIFIES an EXISTING file in the UNAMBIGUOUS adopter-linter basename allowlist (eslint/prettier/biome/ruff/stylelint/markdownlint/shellcheck/tslint/flake8 — NOT pyproject.toml/setup.cfg/package.json, NOT governance configs which are the canonical guard's job per MF-L/debate K6). The insight: an agent 'fixes' a failing lint gate by relaxing the config instead of the code → 'fix the code, not the config'. Design choice = block-any-edit (ECC parity, revisitable; see module docstring). Escape hatches: CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 (session) or <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable (per-repo). User ceremony wires the ADVISORY variant (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1 → allow + systemMessage steer, never blocks). Fail-OPEN on a hook bug; fail-CLOSED (bounded) only on a write tool with no resolvable file path. Raw tool input is never echoed (basename + resolved path only). MIT-attributed re-implementation of ECC scripts/hooks/config-protection.js.",
.claude/settings.json:507:        "_comment": "PLAN-085 Wave E.4 — PostToolUse Bash canonical-edit forensic audit. Advisory only (never blocks); emits canonical_edit_completed breadcrumb when Bash command targets a canonical governance path via write-shape operators (> / >> / tee / sed -i / git checkout). Composition with E.3 PreToolUse interceptor: E.3 blocks at intent, E.4 records at completion.",
.claude/settings.json:559:        "_comment": "PLAN-028 / ADR-056 lifecycle hook. Fires at session boot — audit init + Gate-1 cache warmup + governance health check. Fail-open: any error → allow + breadcrumb. Kill-switch: CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0.",
.claude/settings.json:583:        "_comment": "PLAN-179 W1-b [amendment r1-C3]: Constraint Pinning PRIMARY channel. On a post-compaction session start (matcher 'compact' — the hook ALSO re-checks source == 'compact' in-process, never trusting the matcher alone), re-states the pinned governance constraints from the CODE constant _lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS (r1-C5 — never read from a .md at runtime, so it cannot be evicted by the summarizer) via additionalContext. RULES, not pointers: the PostCompact reinject hook is the REINFORCEMENT channel, this is the primary one, so pinning does not depend on the still-open W0-1 PostCompact channel verdict. ADVISORY, fail-OPEN, never blocks; emits NO audit event (the action is not yet in _KNOWN_ACTIONS — registration is a follow-up ceremony). Kill-switch: CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0 (deliberately NOT the shared CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY — PLAN-179 §8.8: turning off the continuity snapshot must not silently disarm the governance floor).",
.claude/settings.json:590:            "statusMessage": "Pinning governance constraints after compaction..."
.claude/settings.json:696:            "statusMessage": "Snapshotting governance state before compaction..."
.claude/settings.json:703:        "_comment": "PLAN-135 W2 H1 (ADR-153): PostCompact governance reinjection — after compaction, reads the PreCompact snapshot from the plan scratchpad and reinjects governance POINTERS (active PLAN, execution-unit position, Gate-1 re-read reminder, pending ceremonies) via additionalContext. POINTERS ONLY, never file contents (injection surface). ADVISORY, fail-OPEN. Emits closed-enum compaction_context_reinjected. Kill: CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0.",
