templates/settings/settings.stack.otel.json:2:  "_comment": "CEO Orchestration — OTEL OPT-IN telemetry stack (PLAN-135 W5 / O10). OPT-IN, NOT default-on. Installed ONLY when install.sh is run with --stack otel (turbo-style opt-in, like settings.stack.node.json and settings.stack.sandbox.json). NOT registered by settings.base.json or any default install. This fragment turns ON Claude Code's NATIVE OpenTelemetry emission and points it at the LOCAL loopback sink (.claude/scripts/otel-local-sink.py) — NO egress. Positioning per ADR-087-AMEND-1: audit-log.jsonl = tamper-evident truth (canonical governance record); OTel = dashboard (convenient queryable panel). Consume-native (the harness emits OTel; we sink it locally) != emit-native (ADR-087 still refuses the framework emitting its OWN spans alongside the audit log). See docs/otel-integration.md + the ADR.",
templates/settings/settings.user.json:2:  "_comment": "CEO Orchestration - USER ceremony settings. GENERATED FILE, do not hand-edit: every hook registration, env key and top-level value below is DERIVED from templates/settings/settings.base.json by .claude/scripts/gen-settings-user-template.py, applying the subtraction declared in the `_derivation` key of this same file. To change what the user profile carries, edit `_derivation` and re-run the generator with --write; CI re-runs it with --check and reddens on any drift. The rule the exclusions follow is stated once, in `_derivation.criterion`, and every excluded hook carries its own class, reason and evidence. Retained entries are byte-identical to the base template, including their `_comment` annotations, except where `_derivation.matcher_overrides` or `_derivation.annotation_overrides` declares a difference and says why. All hook FILES are still copied to disk by install.sh, so validate-governance.sh REQUIRED_FILES stay satisfied; an omitted hook is simply never registered, and is therefore dormant for the no-GPG user profile.",
