templates/settings/settings.base.json:2:  "_comment": "CEO Orchestration — BASE hooks (universal, stack-agnostic). Always installed. Stack-specific hooks like tsc+vitest live in settings.stack.<name>.json and are merged in by install.sh via --stack flag. The check-agent-spawn hook is CORE to the protocol — do not remove. Session 75 Codex Finding 2 parity-up with dogfood .claude/settings.json — this template ships ALL active governance hooks the framework runs (currently ~16+: canonical-edit, skill-patch, scratchpad-scope, budget, confidence-gate, output-safety, arbitration-kernel, plan-edit Edit|Write|MultiEdit, tier-policy, read-injection, MCP-response, webfetch-injection, subagent-fabrication, skill-reference-read, skill-bootstrap-post, fluency-nudge). Parity is enforced by .claude/hooks/tests/test_template_dogfood_parity.py. An adopter who wants minimal posture can hand-edit post-install — but the parity test will then warn on update.",
