# Codex CLI version pin — PLAN-081 Phase 6 / R1 C5 BLOCKING per TDE MF-6
#
# Format: semver range. release.yml step 15 + scripts/local/pair-rail-gate.sh
# pre-flight assert that `codex --version` resolves to a version in this range.
# Pin update ceremony: requires Phase 4-bis re-run + GPG sign + ADR amendment
# IF catch_rate shifts >5pp on the locked corpus.
#
# Initial range chosen to cover the Phase 0A SPIKE-VERDICT.md baseline.
#
# v1.16.0 update (Phase 6-bis 2026-05-11 S101-cont): widened upper bound
# to <0.131.0 so Owner's actual binary at codex-cli 0.130.0 is in-range.
# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol, this widening does NOT trigger Phase
# 4-bis re-run because no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken
# yet (initial corpus run is itself part of v1.16.0 GA scope). If post-GA
# the promotion-gate run shows catch_rate shift >5pp on 0.130.x vs
# 0.128.x baseline, ADR-111 amendment + corpus re-run triggers.
#
# PLAN-142 update (S246 2026-06-19): widened upper bound to <0.140.0 so the
# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.139.0 is in-range — the migration that restored
# the pair-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin
# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain
# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per
# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check
# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.
#
# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to
# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the
# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are
# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED
# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an
# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a
# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release
# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).
# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md
# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose
# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`
# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|
# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;
# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869
# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner
# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).
#
# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to
# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump
# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already
# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0
# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release
# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182
# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json, re-pinned in this same pack:
# payload sha256 19c4f144... for 0.147.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity
# recorded from the platform artifact) remains the real supply-chain gate;
# this semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.
# Locked-corpus catch_rate check (ADR-111 §2): Owner elects run-vs-defer at
# pack signing, recorded in the SENT-S318 sentinel Scope.

# PLAN-189 update (S352 2026-09-15): widened upper bound to <0.155.0 so the
# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.154.0 is in-range. The rail was pinned at
# 0.147.0 while the global CLI had moved SEVEN releases ahead, so every rail
# round ran on a revisor older than the one the Owner uses interactively.
# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase
# 4-bis re-run: no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED
# CONSEQUENCE: this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken before
# and after this commit are NOT comparable (S352 rule: re-test on a new
# generation, instrument intact). The 93/93/91 validity series measured in
# S352 was taken under 0.147.0.

# PLAN-189 update (S356 2026-09-18, pack codex-pin-0155): widened upper bound
# to <0.156.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.155.0 is in-range. 0.155.0
# was published to npm on 2026-09-17; with the ADR-182 exact-version payload
# manifest the pair-rail went fail-CLOSED in this repo (`--verify-codex-pin`
# -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch) until this re-pin. LOWER BOUND
# UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape), executed
# OUTSIDE any open release window: GA v1.4.0 was cut 2026-09-15 and
# v1.4.1-rc.1 is cut only AFTER this commit. Per ADR-111
# §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase 4-bis re-run:
# no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE
# (same as S352): this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken
# before and after this commit are NOT comparable. The payload manifest
# (re-pinned in this same pack: payload sha256 b0b14f9c... for
# 0.155.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity recorded from the PLATFORM
# artifact per ADR-182 §5 step 2) remains the real supply-chain gate; this
# semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.
# Doctrine (S355): the Codex CLI is a SHA-pinned substrate — every Codex
# upgrade requires this re-pin BEFORE any release cut; never a casual
# `npm update -g`.

# PLAN-193 update (S357 2026-09-23, pack codex-pin-0156): widened upper bound
# to <0.157.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.156.1 is in-range. 0.156.1
# was published to npm on 2026-09-23 as a hotfix of 0.156.0 (never pinned
# here). With the ADR-182 exact-version payload manifest, installing it before
# this re-pin closes the pair-rail (measured 2026-09-23 against the Owner's
# installed 0.156.1: `--verify-codex-pin` -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch),
# so the ceremony refuses to sign unless the installed payload already hashes
# to the sha256 pinned below. LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0
# (widen-upper-only; raising it past 0.139.0 would put the Codex host-adapter
# fixtures, recorded under codex-cli 0.139.0, out of range). Landed only AFTER
